{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.PhragmenLindelof"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.differentiableOn_comp_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.differentiableOn_comp_inv","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonTransport.lean#L57-L69","doc":"**Inversion preserves holomorphy on the open half-plane.** If `g` is\nholomorphic on `{re > 0}`, so is its precomposition with inversion\n`w ↦ g w⁻¹`. The analyticity half of the Watson `z ↦ 1/z` change of\nvariables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.inv_re_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.inv_re_pos","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonTransport.lean#L49-L55","doc":"**The open right half-plane is invariant under inversion.**\n`z⁻¹.re = z.re / normSq z`, so `0 < z.re ⇒ 0 < z⁻¹.re`. Inversion carries\nthe Watson domain to itself, swapping the ends `0 ↔ ∞`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}